.\n\nCrew cooperation: A leadership qualities but sometimes not good at criticism; B can be uncooperative; C creates positive atmosphere but egocentric and communication difficulty; D arrogant, weak leadership.\n\nProfessional communication: B can be grumpy/uncooperative; A sometimes not good at taking criticism; C difficulty communicating ideas; D arrogant.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously; A leadership; B unknown; C positive atmosphere.\n\nOverall, B seems strong on reliability and stress, but has cooperation issues (uncooperative, grumpy). C is reliable, good crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric. D strong technical, responsibility, but arrogance and weak leadership. A strong technical and leadership but unorganized and not good at criticism.\n\nWhich candidate best fits overall? Might be Candidate C because reliability 100%, positive crew atmosphere, quick correct decisions, but communication difficulty could be mitigated. However egocentric and not willing to further education are concerns.\n\nCandidate B's uncooperative could be serious for crew. Candidate D's arrogance and weak leadership also serious.\n\nCandidate A's unorganized and not good at criticism could affect reliability.\n\nThus maybe C is best overall? Let's compare B vs C. B: reliability, stress, technical, but uncooperative. C: reliability, decision quality, positive crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric. Which is more severe? Uncooperative may affect safety more than communication difficulty? Both matter. Egocentric may affect teamwork. Positive atmosphere suggests good cooperation despite egocentric? Hard.\n\nWe need to make an argument. Could ask other panel members for more info on candidate B's uncooperativeness severity, or candidate C's communication difficulty. But we can also make a contribution now.\n\nWe should reference Agent 3's recommendation of B and either support or challenge. Let's challenge, propose C as stronger